{#-
  The outer shell of every page: <head>, header, footer.
  Page front matter it understands:
    title / title_key, description / description_key
    meta_title_key / metaTitle  a longer title for search results and link previews (<title>, og:title); the page's
                  heading, breadcrumbs, share buttons and site search keep `title` (see _data/eleventyComputed.js)
    title_suffix_key  the text key added after the title in <title> (default site.title_suffix, "A.A. Area 09");
                  no suffix when the title is longer than 55 characters, so search results don't cut it off.
                  A section's own suffix (the Forum pages' prf.title_suffix) also follows og:title, whatever the length
    accent        colour name for the page (ocean, coral, sage, iris, …)
    styles        extra stylesheets   e.g. ["/assets/vendor/leaflet/leaflet.css"]
    headInclude   a partial rendered inside <head> (e.g. image preloads): "partials/home-head.njk"
    jsText        extra data/text keys the page's scripts read from MSCA.t
    scripts       extra scripts (loaded with defer, before Alpine starts)
    bodyClass     extra classes on <body>
    noindex       true to keep a page out of search engines (and out of the site search); such a page (and the
                  404 page) gets no canonical or hreflang links
    altNoindex    true when the same page in the other language is noindex: no hreflang alternates are linked
                  (set automatically for the English Delegate's Corner posts, see _data/eleventyComputed.js)
    searchExclude true to keep a page out of the site search only (past one-off events are left out automatically)
    source        the file volunteers edit to change this page, for the footer's "Edit" link (see _data/eleventyComputed.js)
    ogImage       path to a link-preview image (default: the site's picture, social-card.jpg, or social-card-es.jpg on
                  Spanish pages)
    ogImageWidth / ogImageHeight / ogImageType  that image's size in pixels and type (image/jpeg), when known: the
                  first share of a link then shows the picture at once
    ogImageAlt / og_image_alt_key  what that image shows (or the text key that says it), for screen readers on social
                  sites (the default picture uses site.og_image_alt)
  Site search (Pagefind): the page title and any extra words in data/text/common.csv under
  "search.kw.<English path>" (e.g. search.kw./newcomers/) are weighted so the page itself ranks first,
  together with searchAlso (front matter, and the short forms of a district's number: _data/eleventyComputed.js).
-#}
{%- set L = lang -%}
{%- set lc = L.code -%}
{%- set siteName = "site.name" | t(L) -%}
{%- set isHome = page.url == "/" or page.url == "/es/" -%}
{%- set homeTitle = "site.home_title" | t(L) -%}
{#- Search results and link previews: the meta title (or the page title); the home page has its own. A short title gets
    " · A.A. Area 09" (or the page's title_suffix_key); one over 55 characters stands alone, so it is not cut off. -#}
{%- set coreTitle = metaTitle or title -%}
{%- set titleSuffix = (title_suffix_key or "site.title_suffix") | t(L) -%}
{%- set shortCore = (coreTitle | strip | length) <= 55 -%}
{%- set pageTitle = (coreTitle + (" · " + titleSuffix if (shortCore and titleSuffix) else "")) if (coreTitle and not isHome) else homeTitle -%}
{#- Link previews show og:title as the card's headline: a section's own suffix stays on it ("Save the date · Pacific
    Regional Forum 2028"), while the generic " · A.A. Area 09" is left to og:site_name. -#}
{%- set ogTitle = ((coreTitle + (" · " + titleSuffix if (title_suffix_key and titleSuffix) else "")) if (coreTitle and not isHome) else homeTitle) | strip -%}
{%- set enPath = page.url if lc == "en" else (page.url | altUrl(L)) -%}
{%- set searchable = not (noindex or searchSkip) -%}
{%- set searchTitle = ((title if (title and not isHome) else homeTitle)) | strip -%}
{#- For the site search: Pagefind reads a straight apostrophe as part of the word ("Delegate's" → "delegates") and a
    typographic one as a break ("Delegate’s" → "delegate"). A page's own name is indexed with the typographic one, so
    "delegate" finds the Delegate's Corner; an archived post's title with the straight one, so for a single word
    ("delegate", "delegado") the 57 posts do not all come before the hub pages. A post is still found by its title. -#}
{%- set indexTitle = (searchTitle | replace("’", "'")) if searchType == "post" else (searchTitle | replace("'", "’")) -%}
{%- set desc = description or ("site.description" | t(L)) -%}
{%- set alt = page.url | altUrl(L) -%}
{#- Search engines: a noindex page (and the 404 page) names no canonical address and no language alternates;
    a page whose other-language copy is noindex names only itself. -#}
{%- set indexable = not (noindex or page.url == "/404.html") -%}
<!doctype html>
{#- data-alt: this page in the other language (the installed app's start below); data-no-auto-reload: a page with a form
    the app never reloads by itself (front matter noAutoReload, pwa.js) -#}
<html lang="{{ L.htmlLang }}" data-lang="{{ lc }}" data-base="{{ site.base }}"{% if alt and page.url not in ["/404.html", "/offline/", "/es/offline/"] %} data-alt="{{ alt }}"{% endif %}{% if noAutoReload %} data-no-auto-reload{% endif %} class="scroll-smooth">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  {#- The installed app starts at …?source=app (site.webmanifest: its start page and shortcuts; nothing else carries it):
      it opens in the language of the last page read on this device (pwa.js keeps it; the browser's language at the first start),
      then the ?source=app is dropped from the address. -#}
  <script>(function(){try{var h=document.documentElement,s=location.search;if(!/[?&]source=app(&|$)/.test(s))return;var w=null;try{w=localStorage.getItem("msca-lang")}catch(e){}if(w!=="en"&&w!=="es")w=/^es\b/i.test((navigator.languages&&navigator.languages[0])||navigator.language||"")?"es":"en";var a=h.getAttribute("data-alt");if(w!==h.getAttribute("data-lang")&&a){location.replace((h.getAttribute("data-base")||"/").replace(/\/$/,"")+a);return}history.replaceState(history.state,"",location.pathname+s.replace(/([?&])source=app(&|$)/,function(m,p,n){return n?p:""}).replace(/[?&]$/,"")+location.hash)}catch(e){}})();</script>
  {#- the page's and the whole site's fingerprints (scripts/build-pwa.mjs fills them in): an open page compares them with
      the published ones to bring itself up to date (pwa.js) -#}
  <meta name="msca-build" content="__MSCA_BUILD__">
  <meta name="msca-page" content="__MSCA_PAGE__">
  <title>{{ pageTitle | strip }}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ desc | strip | truncate(300) }}">
  {%- if not indexable %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  {%- else %}
  {#- lets search results and Discover show the page's picture (a flyer, the Forum photo) large, not as a small thumbnail #}
  <meta name="robots" content="max-image-preview:large">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ page.url | absUrl(site.url + '/') }}">
  {%- if not altNoindex %}
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="{{ L.htmlLang }}" href="{{ page.url | absUrl(site.url + '/') }}">
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="{{ 'es' if lc == 'en' else 'en' }}" href="{{ alt | absUrl(site.url + '/') }}">
  <link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="{{ (alt if lc == 'es' else page.url) | absUrl(site.url + '/') }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endif %}
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#2ea3dd">
  {#- Drive serves flyer images reliably only without a Referer; also keeps visitors' paths private. #}
  <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ siteName }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ ogTitle }}">
  <meta property="og:description" content="{{ desc | strip | truncate(200) }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ page.url | absUrl(site.url + '/') }}">
  <meta property="og:locale" content="{{ 'es_US' if lc == 'es' else 'en_US' }}">
  {#- a page without a picture of its own gets the site's picture in the page's language #}
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ (ogImage or ('/assets/img/social-card-es.jpg' if lc == 'es' else '/assets/img/social-card.jpg')) | absUrl(site.url + '/') }}">
  {%- if not ogImage %}
  {#- the default picture: scripts/build-social-card.py draws it at 1200 × 630, so previews need not fetch it first #}
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  <meta property="og:image:type" content="image/jpeg">
  {%- else %}
  {%- if ogImageWidth and ogImageHeight %}
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ ogImageWidth }}">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ ogImageHeight }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if ogImageType %}
  <meta property="og:image:type" content="{{ ogImageType }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- set ogImageText = ogImageAlt or ("" if ogImage else ("site.og_image_alt" | t(L))) %}
  {%- if ogImageText %}
  <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ ogImageText | strip }}">
  {%- endif %}
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  {%- if ogImageText %}
  <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="{{ ogImageText | strip }}">
  {%- endif %}
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon-32.png" sizes="32x32">
  {%- if site.appOn %}
  {#- The installable app (README "The app"): one manifest for both languages; the home-screen icon of iPhones and
      iPads in the page's language (scripts/build-pwa.mjs draws it and swaps the build time for its hash); the same
      short name under the icon whatever the language -#}
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/img/app/apple-touch-icon-{{ lc }}.png?v={{ site.build.ms }}">
  <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest">
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="{{ 'app.short_name' | t(L) }}">
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="default">
  {%- else %}
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
  {%- endif %}
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/outfit-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/inter-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/site.css?v={{ site.build.ms }}">
  {%- for href in styles %}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ href }}{% if href.startsWith('/') and not href.startsWith('//') %}{{ '&' if '?' in href else '?' }}v={{ site.build.ms }}{% endif %}">
  {%- endfor %}
  {#- The shared search matcher, then page scripts, then the site script, then Alpine plugins, then Alpine: all deferred, so they run in this order. #}
  <script defer src="/assets/js/search.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  {%- for src in scripts %}
  {#- the site's own scripts carry the build time too, so a visitor's browser never keeps an old copy after a deploy;
      `npm run build` then swaps it for a hash of each file (scripts/asset-hash.mjs), so an unchanged file keeps its address #}
  <script defer src="{{ src }}{% if src.startsWith('/') and not src.startsWith('//') %}{{ '&' if '?' in src else '?' }}v={{ site.build.ms }}{% endif %}"></script>
  {%- endfor %}
  <script defer src="/assets/js/app.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  {#- the installable app: service worker, updating open pages, "Install the app" (also switches an installed copy off) #}
  <script defer src="/assets/js/pwa.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  {#- the libraries too: asset-hash.mjs gives each the hash of its file, so a library update never meets an old copy #}
  <script defer src="/assets/vendor/alpine-collapse.min.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  <script defer src="/assets/vendor/alpine-focus.min.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  <script defer src="/assets/vendor/alpine-intersect.min.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  <script defer src="/assets/vendor/alpine-persist.min.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  <script defer src="/assets/vendor/alpine.min.js?v={{ site.build.ms }}"></script>
  {#- Structured data for search engines. The Organization on every page: one @id, and its name in the other language
      among the alternate names, so the English and Spanish pages describe the same Area; its registered name (the one
      the About page shows, about.glance_legal_value) ties it to "Alcoholics Anonymous"; the address only when
      mailing_city in data/settings.csv reads "City, ST 12345" (_data/site.js). The WebSite, which tells search results
      the site's name, only on the English home page: Google reads it at the root of the domain only. -#}
  {%- set altNames = [] -%}
  {%- for n in ("site.alt_names" | t(L)).split("|") %}{% if n | trim %}{% set _ = altNames.push(n | trim) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Organization",
    "@id": site.url + "/#organization",
    "name": siteName,
    "legalName": "about.glance_legal_value" | t(L),
    "alternateName": [("site.name" | t(L.other))].concat(altNames),
    "url": site.url + "/",
    "description": "site.description" | t(L),
    "logo": site.url + "/assets/img/logo/logo-en-512.png",
    "email": site.email_webmaster,
    "address": site.postalAddress
  } | json | safe }}</script>
  {%- if page.url == "/" %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebSite",
    "@id": site.url + "/#website",
    "url": site.url + "/",
    "name": siteName,
    "alternateName": altNames,
    "inLanguage": ["en", "es"],
    "publisher": { "@id": site.url + "/#organization" }
  } | json | safe }}</script>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- include "partials/i18n-js.njk" %}
  {#- Always include (an empty partial when there is none): async shortcodes such as the home hero
      preload are dropped when the include sits inside {% if %}. #}
  {%- include (headInclude or "partials/empty.njk") %}
</head>
<body class="min-h-dvh bg-white {{ bodyClass }}" style="{{ (accent or 'ocean') | accent }}">
  <a href="#main" class="skip-link">{{ "a11y.skip" | t(L) }}</a>

  {% include "partials/header.njk" %}

  {#- Site search: archived delegate posts (2020–2023) and event pages count a little less, so the hub page
      (a district, a committee, Minutes …) comes first for general words; they are still found by their own names.
      Meta "type" keeps the internal word (district, committee …): Pagefind also matches meta, so "district 22"
      finds the Spanish district pages too; the search box shows it translated (app.js). The filter of the same
      kind is in the page's language: filters are not matched against the words typed. #}
  {%- set searchKind = (("search.type." + searchType) | tOpt(L)) or ("search.type.page" | t(L)) %}
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="outline-none" {% if searchable %}data-pagefind-body{% if searchType == "post" %} data-pagefind-weight="0.3"{% elif searchType == "event" %} data-pagefind-weight="0.6"{% endif %}{% endif %}
        data-pagefind-meta="title[data-search-title], type[data-search-type]" data-search-title="{{ indexTitle }}" data-search-type="{{ searchType }}"
        data-pagefind-filter="{{ 'search.meta_type' | t(L) }}[data-search-kind]" data-search-kind="{{ searchKind }}">
    {{ content | safe }}
    {%- if searchable and searchType != "event" and searchType != "post" %}
    {#- Not shown: lets the site search rank this hub page (district, committee, documents …) above the many
        event pages and archived posts that mention it, for its own name and keywords. #}
    {%- set searchKw = ("search.kw." + enPath) | tOpt(L) %}
    <div hidden data-pagefind-weight="10">{{ indexTitle }}{% if searchKw %} · {{ searchKw | replace("'", "’") }}{% endif %}{% if searchAlso %} · {{ searchAlso }}{% endif %}</div>
    {%- endif %}
  </main>

  {% include "partials/footer.njk" %}
  {% include "partials/mobile-bar.njk" %}
  {% include "partials/search.njk" %}
  {% include "partials/share-menu.njk" %}
  {%- if site.appOn %}
  {% include "partials/app-install.njk" %}
  {%- endif %}
</body>
</html>
